{:edb/db-before-t 855 :edb/db-after-t 856 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534168 50 #inst "2026-10-06T06:59:59.743Z" 13194139534168 true] [17592186078311 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280081 13194139534168 true] [17592186078312 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280088 13194139534168 true] [17592186078312 1020 #edb/ref 17592186280095 13194139534168 true] [17592186078979 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534168 true] [17592186078979 1100 "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is $x^{2} + y^{2} + 4x - 6y = 3$." 13194139534168 false] [17592186078979 1100 "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4x-6y=3.$" 13194139534168 true] [17592186078979 1145 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4x-6y & =3 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+4x)+({y}^{2}-6y) & =3 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 3y+{3}^{2}) & =3+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+4)+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 3y+9) & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-2))^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={4}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-2,3)$ and its radius is $4.$" 13194139534168 true] [17592186078984 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534168 true] [17592186078984 1100 "Find the radius and center of the circle whose equation is\n\n$x^{2} + y^{2} - 3y = 0$." 13194139534168 false] [17592186078984 1100 "Find the radius and center of the circle whose equation is\n${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-3y=0.$" 13194139534168 true] [17592186078984 1145 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-3y & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+({y}^{2}-3y) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}y+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}) & ={(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect square and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & ={(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x-0)^{2}+{(y-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & ={(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(0,\\frac{3}{2})$ and its radius is $\\frac{3}{2}.$" 13194139534168 true] [17592186280081 1017 #edb/ref 17592186280082 13194139534168 true] [17592186280081 1089 "q-15304" 13194139534168 true] [17592186280081 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534168 true] [17592186280081 1100 "A circle in the Cartesian plane is given by the equation $8x+{x}^{2}-2y=64-{y}^{2}.$ If the circle is written in the standard form $(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2},$ then $a+b+r=$" 13194139534168 true] [17592186280081 1113 #uuid "f65516b8-bb1f-5087-99f2-636aa3137c2b" 13194139534168 true] [17592186280081 1145 "To find the standard form of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x+{x}^{2}-2y & =64-{y}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+8x)+({y}^{2}-2y) & =64 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot y+{1}^{2}) & =64+{4}^{2}+{1}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot y+{1}^{2}) & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & ={9}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & ={9}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-4,b=1$ and $r=9,$ and\n\n$$\na+b+r=-4+1+9=6.\n$$" 13194139534168 true] [17592186280082 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280083 13194139534168 true] [17592186280082 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280084 13194139534168 true] [17592186280082 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280085 13194139534168 true] [17592186280082 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280086 13194139534168 true] [17592186280082 1000 #edb/ref 17592186280087 13194139534168 true] [17592186280082 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534168 true] [17592186280082 1041 "selection" 13194139534168 true] [17592186280082 1104 #edb/ref 17592186280085 13194139534168 true] [17592186280082 1110 #uuid "1e158480-e3c5-5b1a-abac-ad5cf8bdd2ae" 13194139534168 true] [17592186280083 1034 "